12. Those whose 12-lead ECG, physical examination or vital signs examination results are judged by clinicians as abnormal and clinically meaningful;
13. Immunological examinations (hepatitis B surface antigen, hepatitis C virus antibody, human immunodeficiency virus antibody, Treponema pallidum antibody) are positive;
14. Those with abnormal chest radiograph (posterior anterior position) and clinical significance;
15. Women who are pregnant or breastfeeding;
16. Those who have a positive alcohol breath test;
17. Those who have a positive urine drug screening;
18. Those who have a history of drug abuse or drug abuse;
19. People with a history of difficulty in venous blood collection, intolerance to venipuncture, or a history of fainting needles
20. Those who have difficulty swallowing, or have special dietary requirements and cannot follow a uniform diet;
21. The investigator believes that the subject has any other factors that are not suitable for participating in this trial (such as inability to understand the research requirements, poor compliance, infirmity, etc.).

